 "tier1Summary": "South and Central Asia had no single regional turning point this week, but several governments tightened their grip at home. Pakistan's border war with the Afghan [[p:Taliban]] {{note: Islamist movement founded in Kandahar in 1994 under Mullah Omar; it retook Kabul in August 2021.}} ground on, and a Pakistani court jailed two prominent rights lawyers for 10 years. India's opposition took to the streets over the removal of 130 million voters from the rolls. Nepal's new government sacked its police chief after newsroom raids. Brussels called Georgia a candidate \"in name only\". In the Caucasus, Armenia prepares the constitution Baku wants before signing peace, while Azerbaijan feuds with Turkey.\n\nElsewhere, Russia struck Kyiv ahead of Tuesday's Abu Dhabi talks, and the US hit Iranian air defences on Qeshm while saying talks with Tehran continue.",
